# Phase 6 — local env (optional)

Copy to `.env.local` for local Next dev. **Vercel:** set the same keys in **Project → Settings → Environment Variables** (Production + Preview as needed).

## Connect the UI to the Railway API (Vercel + local)

Set these **on the Vercel project** (and optionally here for `npm run dev`):

```bash
# Public HTTPS base URL of your Railway service (no trailing slash)
RAILWAY_API_URL=https://pulse-ui-production-ca4b.up.railway.app

# Same value as RAILWAY_API_SECRET on the Railway service (Bearer token)
RAILWAY_API_SECRET=your-long-random-secret
```

1. In **Railway** → your API service → **Variables** → set **`RAILWAY_API_SECRET`** (generate a long random string).
2. In **Vercel** → your **pulse-ui** (or Phase 6) project → **Settings → Environment Variables**:
   - **`RAILWAY_API_URL`** = your Railway public URL (e.g. `https://….up.railway.app`)
   - **`RAILWAY_API_SECRET`** = **exactly the same** string as on Railway
3. **Redeploy** Vercel (Deployments → … → Redeploy) so serverless routes pick up the new env.

Then **Generate pulse** and **Fetch latest data & send email** call Railway instead of local Python.

Groq / SMTP / Resend stay on **Railway** only (already in Railway env from `.env` pattern). The browser never sees those keys.
